 int end = strlen(str) - 1;
 while (start < end) {
 char temp = str[start];
 str[start] = str[end];
 str[end] = temp;
 start++;
 end--;
 }
}
int main() {
 char word[] = "hello";
 reverse(word);
 printf("%s\n", word);
 return 0;
}
```

##### Output:
```text
olleh
```

```text
Trace of the swap pointers closing in:
h e l l o
^       ^
start=0 end=4   -> swap -> o e l l h

o e l l h
  ^   ^
start=1 end=3   -> swap -> o l l e h

o l l e h
    ^
start=2 end=2   -> start == end, stop
```

